[17592186498134 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498134 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9339d5e1-6245-5bf5-bba6-2750f42458db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498295 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{4}{(s-2)^{3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498295 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498295 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "de1efeda-62c3-5e17-b7cb-b295d6451ef1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498331 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{12}{(s-2)^{4}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498331 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498331 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f22261e4-628e-5669-8943-4998a47f8540" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498359 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{24}{(s-2)^{4}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498359 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498359 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ff0b72cf-c5ca-5854-b15b-0478c4cfc654" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498404 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186497855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498404 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186497923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498404 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186497924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498404 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498404 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498404 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498404 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498404 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186497855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498404 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "64110326-a77e-5f76-b890-3c31d6f5dae0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186497973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498469 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498469 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498469 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186498359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498469 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d796c28f-05c4-5d13-97d9-d47a85425db2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498513 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498513 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332120" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498513 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498513 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ba/ba6fb6239cc146b1fb5fc31300015984826e4ab1fe4061a0bd14ce3b2643569f.png)\n\nConsider a function $f(t)$ for which the graph of the Laplace transform $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be the graph of $L\\{{e}^{t}f(t)\\}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498513 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2ff7cb38-62cd-5c8f-a2e0-afb3c4fd3adf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498513 #edb/ref 1074 "The first shifting theorem states that if\n$L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s),$\nthen\n$L\\{{e}^{at}f(t)\\}=F(s-a).$\n\nThis implies that multiplying a function $f(t)$ by ${e}^{at}$ shifts the corresponding Laplace transform horizontally along the $s$-axis.\n\n- If $a>0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the right.\n\n- If $a<0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the left.\n\nIn our case, to get the graph of $L\\{{e}^{t}f(t)\\},$ we must shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $1$ unit to the right.\n\n![](images/97/97b2ac07998dea2ba0116ae4b1b26bccdc2c6b2a64d99836578c01d5502c61d2.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498560 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498560 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332127" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498560 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498560 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{t}^{n}\\} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}, &  & s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nuse linearity of Laplace transforms and the first shifting theorem to find the Laplace transform of $f(t)=6t+4{t}^{3}{e}^{2t}$ for $s>2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498560 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8828e2f6-2765-54b6-be68-2960b77fe33e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498560 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we apply the linearity properties of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{f(t)\\} & =L\\{6t+4{t}^{3}{e}^{2t}\\} \\\\  & =L\\{6t\\}+L\\{4{t}^{3}{e}^{2t}\\} \\\\  & =6L\\{t\\}+4L\\{{t}^{3}{e}^{2t}\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that, for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{t}^{n}\\} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{t\\} & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ L\\{{t}^{3}\\} & =\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first shifting theorem states that if $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s),$ then $L\\{{e}^{at}f(t)\\}=F(s-a).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nL\\{{t}^{3}{e}^{2t}\\}=\\frac{6}{(s-2)^{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{f(t)\\} & =6L\\{t\\}+4L\\{{t}^{3}{e}^{2t}\\} \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+4\\cdot \\frac{6}{(s-2)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{24}{(s-2)^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis transform is valid for $s>2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498613 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1ca3e022-cc39-56cd-87c5-f311545581d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498613 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186498560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498616 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498616 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2727354f-cd77-55e1-a1d0-cd9c6788d154" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498616 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186221931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498627 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498627 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "657640d3-5628-5d33-809c-aa5fdbf0b2e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498627 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186498513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498639 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186498627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498639 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9646d192-bbba-563e-9982-b0be272fde36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498639 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186304980 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
